From 7ba65c44e5740feccacfc3978d0b00caf98af679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amelie Delaunay <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 16:33:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: stm32: amdf: advertise batched PCM pointer reporting

The STM32 AMDF PCM interface does not guarantee continuously advancing
hardware pointer updates visible to ALSA userspace. The reported position
may advance in batches rather than at burst granularity.

Advertise SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH so userspace is informed that the hardware
pointer may only be updated periodically, for example once per period,
instead of continuously.

This makes the PCM hardware flags reflect the actual pointer reporting
behavior more accurately.

Change-Id: Idfceff3da7df5590fec2404aafd280be53094b00
Signed-off-by: Amelie Delaunay <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/582122
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Olivier MOYSAN <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
Reviewed-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
Tested-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 sound/soc/stm/stm32_amdf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sound/soc/stm/stm32_amdf.c
+++ b/sound/soc/stm/stm32_amdf.c
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ struct stm32_amdf_priv {
 
 static const struct snd_pcm_hardware stm32_amdf_pcm_hw = {
 	.info = SNDRV_PCM_INFO_INTERLEAVED | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BLOCK_TRANSFER |
-		SNDRV_PCM_INFO_MMAP | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_PAUSE,
+		SNDRV_PCM_INFO_MMAP | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_PAUSE | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH,
 	.formats = SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE,
 
 	.channels_min = 1,
